/*
    prototype design pattern is one of the creational design pattern
    It is used when we want to create duplicate of an existing object instead of creating new object from scratch.
    It is highly used in Spring Boot Bean Scopes, Hibernate Caching, and Game Development.
    Definition:Prototype design pattern is used to create duplicate object with same values of existing object without calling constructor.

    why do we need prototype design pattern ?
    1.> Object creation is costly
    2.> Cloning is Faster Than object creation
    3.> Solves performance issue
    4.> Support Shallow copy & deep copy

    Types of cloning
    Type                 Description                             Example
    1.>Shallow copy      Only reference is cloned                Default Clone()
    2.>Deep Copy         Object + all fields Cloned              Custom Clone()

    Where Prototype Design Pattern is Used in Real-Time Projects?
Use Case                            	Example
Spring Framework	                      Bean Scopes (Prototype Scope)
Hibernate	                              Cache Mechanism
Database Connection	                      Connection Pool
Game Development	                      Creating Multiple Characters
   */